ALL LINES:
- Each line starts with a tag (indicator for parsing) and a delimiter (ALWAYS a colon)
- Afterwards, values are written as follows:
    -pairs of values (i.e a framecount and frame id) are indicated by  aXb
    -pairs of values plus a frame are indicated by aXb,c
    -lists of values or value pairs are separated by spaces
    -groups of four or more values are formatted a,b,c,d

MOVE KEY:
framenum; a; the number of frames in an animation
frameorder; axb; the number (a) of a frame (id b) in a row before the next unique frame is displayed
startaltitude: -1 for crouching,  0 for grounded, 1 for aerial

ID: numbered as follows:
type (000-999 representing order in animType enum class), aerial or not (0 or 1), (input (000-991, aligned with a chart),
ordinality (order in sequence, 0 to 9), variant(0-9, representing A-J)

ex: 019004000 represents g4a1A


